WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.069
-For the past eight days
in cities across the country,

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.005
Americans have protested the
recent murder of George Floyd

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.540
at the hands of police.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.975
Many of those protests
have turned violent,

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:11.544
due not to the protesters,

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.879
but to the response
of the police themselves.

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:15.848
Here to comment on that
is one of our writers,

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:19.986
Amber Ruffin, with a segment
called "Amber's Minute of Fury."

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:24.124
♪♪

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.458
-Fool!

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.860
Dang police violence
at these protests!

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.295
What are you doing?!

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.897
Your response to "please stop
unnecessarily hurting us"

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:35.735
is to go to a peaceful protest
and unnecessarily hurt us?

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.604
Your response to
"we think you are too violent"

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.173
is this outfit?

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:43.176
You idiots! "Stop killing
Black people" is so easy.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.945
It's like when they give you
a point on the SATs

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.647
for just writing your name.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.415
But it's clear
some police can't handle that,

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:52.418
so maybe there's an adult
in the room who can go, "Okay.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:54.954
Now, no more killing
Black people. And I mean it."

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.290
And then everyone else can just
be like, "Yeah, you're right."

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.624
Is that possible?

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.960
Oh, wait, wait. The President
is going to talk soon.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.729
He'll save us.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:06.232
-I am mobilizing all available
federal resources,

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:10.570
civilian and military, to stop
the rioting and looting.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.171
-Damn! That --
That doesn't help at all!

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:13.605
This is crazy!

00:01:13.605 --> 00:01:15.542
At least this is
the only emergency

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.209
facing our nation at the moment.

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:18.845
Coronavirus?!

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.914
No one took care of coronavirus?

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.716
Whose job was it? No one's?

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.786
Wow! This is the craziest April
I've ever been a part of.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.587
June?!

00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:31.824
Okay, so, the officer arrested
for killing George Floyd,

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:36.228
Derek Chauvin, had 18 previous
complaints filed against him.

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:37.997
Eighteen?
How is he still policing?

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.866
If you stick your hand
in the pudding

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.068
at The Golden Corral once,
you will never be allowed

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.103
back in there -- so I heard.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:47.540
Being a cop is easier than
eating at The Golden Corral?!

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.841
I'm just kidding.

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:50.944
I've never acted crazy in public
or anything like that,

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.344
because when Black people
do that,

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:53.947
we run the risk
of being murdered.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.215
[ Ding! ]

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:56.949
Now, I know
what you're thinking --

00:01:56.949 --> 00:01:58.351
"Not all cops are bad.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.619
I heard some of them are
kneeling with the protesters."

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:03.822
So, look, I don't like to get
mad at people for trying.

00:02:03.822 --> 00:02:06.826
I don't think that's very nice.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.228
I can see how, on the surface,

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.195
police kneeling
alongside the protesters

00:02:10.195 --> 00:02:13.299
is a nice gesture,
but, um, how do I say this?

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.235
Uh, get up off the ground
and help us!

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:18.638
Train your little friends
to do their job correctly!

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.406
Make it illegal
to kill us without cause

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.642
and then -- and this is where
I think you can really help --

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.976
enforce that law!

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.111
Even if it's your buddy
who breaks it!

00:02:26.111 --> 00:02:28.681
Now, those are my suggestions,
and they're good ones.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.750
You know what's not
a good suggestion?

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.694
Damn it, Joe!
You are not helping!

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.463
I am so sick of you already.

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:45.631
Just keep your mouth shut
until November

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:47.833
and don't say anything racist.

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:49.402
-If you have a problem
figuring out

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:52.505
whether you're for me or Trump,
then you ain't Black.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.507
-Dang it, Joe! I swear to God.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:57.477
If you don't just shut up
and let us vote for you...

00:02:57.477 --> 00:03:00.046
Now, the protests this week have
been rough on the protesters,

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.881
but you know who else
they've been rough on?

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.783
Reporters.
These people have been arrested.

00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:07.086
They've had rubber bullets
shot at them.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.089
This one lady
even got shot on the air.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.958
-We've got plenty of time here.
-Aah! Aah!

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.493
-Are you okay?
-I'm getting shot!

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:16.028
I'm getting --
-Kate? Katie, are you okay?

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:18.565
-Rubber bullets! Rubber bullets!
-And they were shot!

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:22.401
But I'm like, "Don't you know
why everyone is protesting?"

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:25.238
'Cause the police like
to hurt people for no reason.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.873
This is like
going to a bake sale

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.808
and being surprised
when you see muffins.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.444
"M-M-Muffins
at a ba-ba-bake sale?!"

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.012
Yeah, dummy!

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.313
Now, I can remember years ago

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:36.315
when everyone was talking
about stop and frisk.

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:38.217
And I swear to God, I was like,

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:41.086
"It's illegal for cops
to do us like that?"

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:43.623
I'm telling you,
I had experienced it and seen it

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.524
so many times,
it never occurred to me

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:47.626
that that might not be allowed.

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:49.562
So, yeah, the police
might hurt you without cause.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.130
Oh, my God. I almost forgot.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.698
Okay, there was one reporter

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:54.667
who got cuffed
and taken away on air --

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.735
and before you ask,
of course, he was --

00:03:56.735 --> 00:03:58.871
but then he was
back to reporting

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.706
after the commercial break!

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:03.209
Do you know how much resilience
that takes?

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:05.078
Once there was
a spider on my desk,

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:07.213
and I went home for the day.

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:10.049
Oh, hold on. I just heard the
President is going to talk.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.117
He'll save us.

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:16.021
-One law and order.

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:18.457
And that is what it is.
One law.

00:04:18.457 --> 00:04:21.427
We have one beautiful law.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:24.230
-That wasn't helpful at all!
Damn!

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.731
Meanwhile,
in the middle of all this,

00:04:25.731 --> 00:04:28.568
these two idiots
just [bleep] left us here.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:32.205
Cowardly spacemen!
They got to leave the planet.

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.739
I can't even leave my house

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:36.375
because of
coronavirus AND curfew.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.846
But that's okay because
the President is on TV again,

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:43.516
and I bet he's going to do
something really helpful.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:45.918
[ Sirens wailing ]

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:52.525
-Why?! What are you doing?!

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:55.161
You know what? I don't think
he's gonna help us.

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.062
And we are in a dangerous spot

00:04:57.062 --> 00:04:59.265
because this fool
is amping up the rhetoric.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.434
This is a real problem.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:04.236
And for things to change,
we need real leaders.

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:08.207
Leaders who have the courage
to take a stand for our safety.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.909
-I won't traffic
in fear and division.

00:05:10.909 --> 00:05:13.846
I won't fan the flames of hate.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.215
I'll seek to heal
the racial wounds

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.251
that have long plagued
our country,

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:23.022
not use them for political gain.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:25.958
I'll do my job,
and I will take responsibility.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:27.893
I won't blame others.

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:29.929
-Thank you, Joe. Good job.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:32.632
Now back in the basement
until November!

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:34.834
This has been
"Amber's Minute of Fury."

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:38.804
♪♪

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:40.205
-Thank you, Amber Ruffin.

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:42.241
We'll be right back
with Amanda Peet.

